If `ChannelRouter` is deserialized from an older version (or using default values), `channel_fatigue` and `baseline_weights` will be empty vectors. Accessing `self.channel_fatigue[i]` or `self.baseline_weights[i]` will then cause a runtime panic due to out-of-bounds indexing. We should lazily initialize/resize these vectors to `n` if their lengths do not match.

